WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:03.560
Everyone knows how to win.

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:06.340
But only a few know how to lose.

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:08.500
And I say this because recently we had a loss.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:13.929
And that loss was we announced the second
week of May that we wanted to have 100,000

00:00:13.929 --> 00:00:16.209
subs by August 31st.

00:00:16.209 --> 00:00:19.250
And remember, when we announced that we had
about 41,000 subs.

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:21.869
When it ended, we did not hit 100,000 subs.

00:00:21.869 --> 00:00:24.590
We ended with 83, 000 subs.

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:25.710
And it was very disappointing.

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:26.710
We were very annoyed.

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:30.999
We were very frustrated that we didn't hit
the 100,00 subs and then somebody asked the

00:00:30.999 --> 00:00:33.800
question on the YouTube channel on the bottom
and said, "You know what, Pat?

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:37.100
I would really want to know how you handle
a loss."

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:41.100
And I said, "What a great idea to do an episode
on how to handle a loss, because so many times

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.370
everybody talks about doing and motivating
and all this other stuff, but how do you handle

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:45.450
a loss?

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:47.390
So today's episode is going to be all about
that.

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:52.050
Matter of fact, it was so painful that Mario
from the team is still emotional with the

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:53.670
fact that we didn't hit 100,000 subs.

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:57.280
Paul, why don't you show Mario's reaction
here on how emotional he is.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:59.260
Mario, are you going to be okay?

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:00.400
I'm fine.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:01.400
I'm okay.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:02.400
You sure?

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:03.400
Yeah.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:04.400
Alright.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:05.400
Mario's going to be okay.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:06.400
Maybe you can - Mario, let me see this here
real quick.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:07.400
By the way, if you haven't subbed, do him
a favor and subscribe to the channel.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.690
Okay, there you go Mario.

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:10.690
Here's some love.

00:01:10.690 --> 00:01:15.370
Okay, so now, how do we handle a loss as an
entrepreneur?

00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:17.280
There's three things I'll cover here today.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:23.610
One is two different types of goals people
set, two is what do you do when you actually

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:28.409
set up a goal, and then three is how to handle
a loss and how do you debrief when you don't

00:01:28.409 --> 00:01:29.409
achieve your goals.

00:01:29.409 --> 00:01:30.409
So we'll cover those three things.

00:01:30.409 --> 00:01:31.409
Let me start off with the first one.

00:01:31.409 --> 00:01:33.850
What do I mean by there are two different
types of goals?

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:34.850
Okay.

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:39.600
So there are people that set too small of
a goal or too big of a goal.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:40.890
So what is too small of a goal?

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:46.500
Unfortunately, there are a lot of people that
most of their goals become a reality.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:47.510
Most of their goals become a reality.

00:01:47.510 --> 00:01:48.850
And what do I mean by that?

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:51.660
The goal could be hey, I want to have a job.

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:52.790
They land a job.

00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:55.430
Hey I want to have a place to live.

00:01:55.430 --> 00:01:56.970
They get a place to live.

00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:59.470
I want to have three square meals to eat every
day.

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:00.549
They get those meals.

00:02:00.549 --> 00:02:02.060
I want to have a car to drive.

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:03.060
They get a car.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:04.600
I want to one day get married.

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:05.930
They get married.

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:10.979
Everything is, they hit a goal, but it's small
of a goal and they settle.

00:02:10.979 --> 00:02:12.680
So their goals become a reality.

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:14.019
But it's too small of a goal.

00:02:14.019 --> 00:02:20.939
Then the complete opposite is, people who
set way, way too ambitious goals with small

00:02:20.939 --> 00:02:21.939
timelines.

00:02:21.939 --> 00:02:22.939
Let me explain.

00:02:22.939 --> 00:02:23.939
For instance.

00:02:23.939 --> 00:02:25.980
I remember I got out of the Army.

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:27.420
I was 21 years old.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:32.189
I have a picture of this that I took, and
if we were back at home, you know, back in

00:02:32.189 --> 00:02:37.239
Dallas, we would show this here, but I'm back
at home, I would have shown the picture.

00:02:37.239 --> 00:02:40.999
I have a blue shirt, polyester shirt, pretty
pathetic.

00:02:40.999 --> 00:02:42.639
I'm wearing a blue polyester shirt.

00:02:42.639 --> 00:02:49.139
I used to dress like my inspiration was John
Travolta from Saturday Night Fever and Stayin

00:02:49.139 --> 00:02:50.249
Alive.

00:02:50.249 --> 00:02:55.360
So I have this shirt and I'm holding a paper
and I'm in Chicago with two of my friends,

00:02:55.360 --> 00:03:00.249
and on it it says, when I'm going to be a
millionaire, and my date for becoming a millionaire

00:03:00.249 --> 00:03:01.919
was a year after getting out of the Army.

00:03:01.919 --> 00:03:05.010
Now how am I going to become a millionaire
a year after getting out of the Army when

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:07.029
I didn't know how to do anything?

00:03:07.029 --> 00:03:08.780
I knew nothing, right?

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:10.489
And I want to be a millionaire within a year.

00:03:10.489 --> 00:03:12.379
It didn't happen.

00:03:12.379 --> 00:03:13.379
Disappointed.

00:03:13.379 --> 00:03:16.879
Some people want to get married, find a loved
one and have a kid within a week.

00:03:16.879 --> 00:03:20.900
Unless if you marry somebody with a kid, that
is way too ambitious of a goal, right?

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:23.159
Or you say, I want to be a billionaire within
the next two years.

00:03:23.159 --> 00:03:27.689
I get it it and I want you to know that sometimes
people say well Pat, isn't it good to think

00:03:27.689 --> 00:03:28.689
big?

00:03:28.689 --> 00:03:34.590
It is very good to think big, but that goal
must be a goal that if 100% is impossible

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:41.569
for you to hit it and zero is you're guaranteed
to hit it, make sure it's 80%, if that makes

00:03:41.569 --> 00:03:42.579
any sense.

00:03:42.579 --> 00:03:43.709
Make sure it's 80%.

00:03:43.709 --> 00:03:45.140
So what do I mean by that?

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:50.340
You've got $2,000 in savings right now, your
goal is to have $100,000 in savings within

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:51.340
18 months.

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:52.609
I like that.

00:03:52.609 --> 00:03:55.780
You're 168 pounds right now and you want to
get to 148 pounds, lose 20 pounds, in the

00:03:55.780 --> 00:03:57.319
next 60 days.

00:03:57.319 --> 00:03:58.319
That's good.

00:03:58.319 --> 00:04:01.840
If you say I want to lose 20 pounds in a week,
that's not healthy to do that.

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:03.609
But if you say within a month or two, okay,
that's good.

00:04:03.609 --> 00:04:07.299
You can pull that off if you drop certain
things you can get to that weight.

00:04:07.299 --> 00:04:11.669
So again, two types of goals, - too small
of a goal, too big of a goal, you want to

00:04:11.669 --> 00:04:17.000
make sure you set a goal that is reachable,
but it's got to be difficult to reach.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:19.509
It's got to be difficult to reach, yet you
can reach it.

00:04:19.509 --> 00:04:24.340
So you'll kind of get that part when you do
more of these things, you'll eventually figure

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:25.340
it out.

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:29.700
And remember, just like in the world of sports,
no basketball team's ever gone undefeated.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:34.389
The greatest basketball player of all time
is Michael Jordan, and he missed 45% of his

00:04:34.389 --> 00:04:36.810
shots and he lost quite a lot of games.

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:38.780
He wasn't undefeated.

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:41.250
The greatest baseball player of all time was
Babe Ruth.

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:42.680
He hit three out of 10 times.

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:44.300
If you think about it, 10 at best.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:47.080
So don't expect undefeated and perfection.

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:48.080
Okay?

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:50.629
But at the same time, you need to be getting
your hits, you need to be getting your victors,

00:04:50.629 --> 00:04:53.440
you need to be getting your shots, you need
to be scoring, and winning.

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:56.210
So make sure you know exactly how to do that
part with the size of your goal.

00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:57.470
So now let's go to the next part.

00:04:57.470 --> 00:05:00.090
The next part is now, what do I do now?

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:02.699
So let's talk about the process of setting
a goal.

00:05:02.699 --> 00:05:04.629
#1: You set a goal.

00:05:04.629 --> 00:05:06.540
Now what is a goal tied to?

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:08.879
A lot of people say, "I have a goal.

00:05:08.879 --> 00:05:12.280
Generally, to me, when I think about a goal,
I think about a number.

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:13.580
So what's a goal?

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:15.979
Goal is, I want to lose 20 pounds.

00:05:15.979 --> 00:05:17.430
Goal is I want to make 100,000.

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:20.790
Goal is, I want to have 5,000 subs on my YouTube
channel.

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:25.229
Goal is, I want to have $50,000 in savings.

00:05:25.229 --> 00:05:27.169
Goal is tied to a number.

00:05:27.169 --> 00:05:28.539
Goal is tied to a number.

00:05:28.539 --> 00:05:30.000
Goal is generally tied to a number.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.240
So you set a goal, and a number.

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:33.949
So you write those two down.

00:05:33.949 --> 00:05:34.949
Whatever that things is.

00:05:34.949 --> 00:05:35.949
Number 1, Goal, Number.

00:05:35.949 --> 00:05:37.600
So just write this down and go with me.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:40.580
#2: Is your strategy on how to get there.

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:43.040
So goal, number, strategy, how to get there.

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:46.550
I know Paul's typing it here so you're kind
of seeing it on the screen as well.

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:49.289
So goal, number, strategy, how to get there.

00:05:49.289 --> 00:05:53.169
You've got to take a minute and write out
a strategy on how you're going to get to the

00:05:53.169 --> 00:05:54.169
number.

00:05:54.169 --> 00:05:56.140
#3: There's got to be a deadline.

00:05:56.140 --> 00:05:57.900
Goals without deadlines mean nothing.

00:05:57.900 --> 00:06:00.530
Sometimes people say I want to be a millionaire,
but there's no deadline.

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:01.629
You're not going to be a millionaire.

00:06:01.629 --> 00:06:02.729
You're just winging it.

00:06:02.729 --> 00:06:04.030
I want to lose 20 pounds.

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:05.120
By when?

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:06.449
I want to make six figures.

00:06:06.449 --> 00:06:07.630
By when?

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:09.590
I want to have $50,000 in savings.

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:10.590
By when?

00:06:10.590 --> 00:06:11.590
I want to buy my house.

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:12.590
By when?

00:06:12.590 --> 00:06:13.590
Deadline.

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:14.590
Deadline is very, very critical.

00:06:14.590 --> 00:06:15.590
So so far we have what?

00:06:15.590 --> 00:06:19.219
Goal, number, strategy, then you have your
deadline.

00:06:19.219 --> 00:06:20.510
The next thing.

00:06:20.510 --> 00:06:23.439
Next thing I call your ask, your value.

00:06:23.439 --> 00:06:28.009
Meaning what are you asking for - the goal,
and what value are you going to bring for

00:06:28.009 --> 00:06:29.009
that goal?

00:06:29.009 --> 00:06:32.690
What are you exchanging your ask, for your
value?

00:06:32.690 --> 00:06:37.409
Here's what I want, this is the value I'm
willing to bring to make $100,000.

00:06:37.409 --> 00:06:40.000
This is the value I'm willing to bring to
buy my house.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:43.039
This is the value I'm willing to bring to
save $50,000.

00:06:43.039 --> 00:06:45.979
This is the value I'm willing to bring for
me to lose 20 pounds.

00:06:45.979 --> 00:06:46.979
What's the value?

00:06:46.979 --> 00:06:50.800
I'm willing to go to the gym four times a
week, this is the value I'm willing to bring

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:51.800
to make this back.

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:55.009
So the value almost means like how are you
going to prove yourself.

00:06:55.009 --> 00:06:56.190
That's how I take value as.

00:06:56.190 --> 00:07:01.009
So what areas are you going to prove in yourself,
areas of improvement, disciplines, etc.

00:07:01.009 --> 00:07:02.009
Habits.

00:07:02.009 --> 00:07:11.990
So now we have goal, number, strategy, deadline,
your ask, your value, next one is declaring

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:13.360
your intention.

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:14.900
Here's what I mean by declaring your intention.

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:18.969
There's a big difference between you having
a personal trainer that you hire than you

00:07:18.969 --> 00:07:20.210
working out by yourself.

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:21.210
Here's why.

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:23.629
If he says you've got to be there by 6:00
in the morning and you're late by five minutes,

00:07:23.629 --> 00:07:25.410
there's two things that happens in your mind.

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:29.819
One you're saying, I'm paying $150 an hour
and I'm late five minutes - I just lost $10.

00:07:29.819 --> 00:07:31.009
That's what you tell yourself.

00:07:31.009 --> 00:07:32.370
Two, here's what you say.

00:07:32.370 --> 00:07:35.099
Man, I don't want to be late, because I'm
wasting his time.

00:07:35.099 --> 00:07:36.870
He's going to think I'm not serious.

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:37.870
Accountability.

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:39.770
So that's declaring your intention.

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:43.639
When you say you want to do something, you've
got to tell the world about it, the world

00:07:43.639 --> 00:07:45.120
holds you accountable.

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:46.150
The world holds you accountable.

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:48.810
A lot of people want to get into shape, but
they're afraid of saying what they look like

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:49.810
today.

00:07:49.810 --> 00:07:50.819
Hold yourself accountable.

00:07:50.819 --> 00:07:57.699
You'd be amazed at how much that positive
pressure can get you to do something in yourself.

00:07:57.699 --> 00:07:59.770
You know, hey, what is your intentions this
year?

00:07:59.770 --> 00:08:02.889
Well, we're playing this year to win the Super
Bowl and we're doing everything we can to

00:08:02.889 --> 00:08:03.889
get to the big show.

00:08:03.889 --> 00:08:05.590
We're doing everything we can to get to the
big show.

00:08:05.590 --> 00:08:06.719
You know what's important to us?

00:08:06.719 --> 00:08:08.289
We're going after the big show.

00:08:08.289 --> 00:08:12.220
And you'll see the difference between how
MBA players sometimes they'll say, Do you

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:15.039
think if you finish your career without a
championship, do you think your legacy is

00:08:15.039 --> 00:08:16.099
still intact?

00:08:16.099 --> 00:08:17.099
Yes!

00:08:17.099 --> 00:08:18.099
Okay.

00:08:18.099 --> 00:08:19.150
Then that's not their goal.

00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:22.009
Now you see somebody else saying, You think
you're career's intact if you don't win any

00:08:22.009 --> 00:08:23.009
championships?

00:08:23.009 --> 00:08:24.289
No, I have to win a championship.

00:08:24.289 --> 00:08:25.500
That's declaring intention.

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:27.370
Then you've got to go get it.

00:08:27.370 --> 00:08:30.650
And fans love it, and there's pressure.

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:34.220
Then you practice, you train hard, you've
got to make sure you come through.

00:08:34.220 --> 00:08:36.770
And the last one is execution, period.

00:08:36.770 --> 00:08:41.020
So now you have your goals and numbers, your
strategy which is your how-to, your deadline

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:46.430
which is clear on when you want to hit it,
and typically deadlines to me, I like 90-day

00:08:46.430 --> 00:08:47.430
deadlines.

00:08:47.430 --> 00:08:48.640
I'm a 90-day type of guy.

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:52.220
I know a lot of times we can do 30 days or
one week, and what I'm going to do this week.

00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:53.580
You always have your days and weeks.

00:08:53.580 --> 00:08:56.140
On Sunday nights I'd prepare for my entire
week.

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:58.920
But say this is a 90-day goal we're talking
about, and you have a deadline.

00:08:58.920 --> 00:09:05.380
And it's your ask, your value, and then you
declare your intention, and it's execution.

00:09:05.380 --> 00:09:08.670
Okay, so we said now on what happens with
that.

00:09:08.670 --> 00:09:14.500
Now let's talk about the complete ourselves,
what we did and then what you don't do when

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:15.500
you come back.

00:09:15.500 --> 00:09:21.680
So now, for us it was our goal, the number
was 100,000 subs was what we wanted to do,

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:22.680
right?

00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:27.380
Our strategy was we were going to produce
one video, which was called Good Voice, Bad

00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:33.020
Voice, which on Facebook it did very well
and ended up getting 1.1 million views and

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:38.370
I think on YouTube it ended up getting 96,000
views or something like that.

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:42.200
So that was one of our strategies and our
strategy was our two videos a week that we

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:47.070
were doing and with the hopes that with the
following, every video we were going to execute

00:09:47.070 --> 00:09:50.310
and say hey, please subscribe and please invite
other people to subscribe to the channel,

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:54.600
help us out, and by the way, I want to take
a moment and just thank all of you that really

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:58.760
helped out this channel because quite frankly,
we would be at zero subs if it wasn't for

00:09:58.760 --> 00:09:59.760
you.

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:04.790
We wouldn't even be at the 80 some thousand
subs, I think we're at 89,000 subs when you're

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:05.910
watching this.

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:09.440
We would not be if it wasn't for you sharing
this video with other people and inviting

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:13.270
other people to join, emailing your friends,
sharing it on your social media, so from me

00:10:13.270 --> 00:10:16.130
to you, I want to thank you for helping us
out.

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:21.340
But you heard one part of our strategy was
every single video, you're going to see this.

00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:22.340
Please subscribe.

00:10:22.340 --> 00:10:23.470
So we made the ask.

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:25.540
Part of the strategy was make the ask.

00:10:25.540 --> 00:10:26.880
We brought you the value.

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:29.260
We asked please, will you subscribe to the
channel.

00:10:29.260 --> 00:10:30.500
And we gave you value.

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:31.500
Ask, value.

00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:32.500
Ask, value.

00:10:32.500 --> 00:10:33.500
Ask, value.

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:36.310
Okay, so strategy was right there.

00:10:36.310 --> 00:10:43.290
Deadline was August 31, then after the deadline,
it was declaring intention, which we said,

00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:52.020
"Hey, we want to get to 100,000 subs by August
31 and then there was execution.

00:10:52.020 --> 00:10:56.090
Now obviously, we didn't execute perfectly
because we didn't get to 100,000 subs.

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:59.721
